{"id":"20260825T185324.578895050Z-c21d7602","time":"2026-08-25T18:53:24.57889505Z","session_id":"session-20260825T184812.829903860Z","task_id":"task-1787683692830141953","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  There is no way to ask why a specific piece of governing knowledge exists.\n\nAdd to internal/architect the exported function:\n\n    func RunWhy(caller Caller, domain, id string) (string, error)\n\nGiven an id it resolves the rule through the supplied Caller's awareness_resolve tool and returns a report carrying what the graph holds about it. An empty id is an error naming the expected form. The class is not assumed from the id: an architect copies whatever they were shown, so a rule held under another kind must still be found rather than refused on a guess, and an id carrying a class prefix must resolve to the same rule as the bare one, with no prefix sent to Sensei. The domain scopes the query when non-empty and is omitted when empty. An id the graph holds nothing under is an error naming that id.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei holds an active high-severity invariant requiring retrieval to be selected by the question, bounded explicitly, and to report an empty answer rather than widen the search. (RunWhy retrieval and not-found behavior) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] internal/architect/run.go defines Caller.CallTool and existing architect helpers conditionally add domain only when it is non-empty. (internal/architect/run.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The Sensei MCP client exposes structuredContent through ToolResult.Structured and converts tool refusals into errors carrying Sensei's reason. (internal/sensei/mcp.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Existing repository code strips graph class prefixes before sending identifiers back to Sensei because prefixed identifiers otherwise produce dangling references. (internal/decision/record.go normaliseID and its tests) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The current command registry and TUI dispatch contain no /why route, and command routing is outside this requested implementation slice. (internal/command/command.go and internal/tui/model.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The scoped Sensei preflight examined both planned files, classified the change as low risk with local blast radius, and found no directly anchored governing rule for those files. (internal/architect/run.go and internal/architect/run_test.go) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: bounded-knowledge-gap\n"}
